course: dictionary
lesson: 11457
title: Words that praise
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Admirable is an adjective. It describes something that deserves praise and respect because it is very good. When you admire someone, you think they are great. «Mia read to her little brother every night for a month. Her patience was admirable.» Patience is a good quality, so admirable tells us it is very good and worth praising.
explain: Use the clues around the word. What is being described? Is it a good action, a good quality or a good effort? In the sentence above, it is patience. To check your meaning, swap in "very good and worth praising" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Admirable can describe courage, honesty, kindness or effort. A teacher might write, «Your effort this term has been admirable.» That is praise for your hard work.
fact: Admirable is an adjective: admirable, more admirable, most admirable.
fact: «Admirable» means deserving praise and respect; very good.
fact: We use admirable for good qualities such as honesty, courage and kindness.
fact: «An admirable effort» means someone tried very hard and deserves praise.
fact: Context clues, such as the word «patience» in the sentence, can help you check the meaning of a word like admirable.
exercise: «The firefighter ran into the smoke to save the cat. Her courage was admirable.» What does admirable mean here? | *Deserving praise and respect | Funny and silly | Frightening and dangerous | Quiet and hidden
exercise: Find and copy the word that means worth praising: «Tom gave an admirable speech, even though he was nervous.» | gave | speech | *admirable | nervous
exercise: Which action is most likely to be admirable? | Hiding your homework | *Sharing your lunch with a friend who forgot theirs | Breaking a friend's pencil on purpose | Shouting at the referee
test: Which word has the same meaning as admirable? | Ordinary | Sleepy | *Praiseworthy | Dreadful
test: «Your kindness to the new girl was admirable.» What does admirable tell us about the kindness? | It is ordinary and forgotten | It is boring and unfinished | *It is very good and deserves praise | It is very bad and should be hidden
exam: Which is the correct way to compare two very good efforts? | admirabler | *more admirable | admirablest | most admirable
